Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"f1b1e80b-9cfa-0e4b-bb3a-781c5c030db2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f6478a92-871c-3641-8ded-5a154d22ae71"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"32077b2e-f9a1-0947-8bf3-97d188e70f97"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"c434cfd9-1812-2848-9603-a7827dcaed6a"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aa8794a7-1902-5b43-9407-f949be2a529b"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a304ca0c-c4b5-eb4a-8fae-060e8dd4d5c5"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7fe5dc3e-1a10-ac4e-8f68-50a5e3d651e2"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e17808ad-8525-b040-96c0-1e5b5178ae8a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8e948ac5-078f-544c-884e-e7264b470de9"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2137043e-0566-884c-a823-729643dd58ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c61f22ef-04b6-114a-ac53-5ac8fc7a4aaa"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"94e336c1-e180-eb4a-92c2-f00802e7948a"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a3ec2ca5-8ae3-8c4c-a904-95fbcf931038"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"d90d871b-7bd6-e34c-98d7-37055cb486b7"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"6869e485-7bc6-394e-b2fd-9d90812a10f1"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c38b0b43-f927-1740-b099-d23004be7530"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"82bf1e54-\
987d-bc4e-800b-095b011d5133"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"1653902f-9019-3645-9ec7-18803aa38670"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fe6c236a-9394-0746-9bed-c06304cfddf9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"ac25852e-\
ae21-ff45-88c1-bc50f23325db"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"e69f4032-37e4-d24f-8f90-cc01335c3d8e"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"be4196fd-a0ea-ab47-b07e-39ffa8dc02d9"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"3b1c4072-e2ce-964b-994b-9b5ce45ea871"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"1e98532e-a5d5-3047-a051-b8dede2fb148"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d7900ef0-1b94-8c41-af47-8bb44ffcab6d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"2b269e8f-\
d498-8c47-bb57-4ac21eeeb7db"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"6d83667f-d314-8242-a65c-1b62454e2500"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c99265be-cbd7-c346-a753-401db5fbf856"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"742369e9-\
ce24-3643-b2e9-ab89b30afd47"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"0c98c103-37ad-fa49-bef9-bd1cc1109fcf"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"39769af6-2fd8-a54f-98e8-a2da536efbba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"9ced0705-\
e237-ab4e-b0a1-32e880dc957e"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"a771bbe4-8d4a-d542-aa2e-57a4163c979d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f1798763-f802-0f46-9753-20085cedd1cd"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"ea2fb929-2e24-3e44-8005-f9e1affad533"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4c3d30aa-37c2-e844-b1bd-64d7ec4331ef"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"45d3e076-2696-b543-a4ca-683e152e8591"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cf004b35-e19c-734f-82af-f7eaf5213d3f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6bb94623-6901-1042-90ae-e981339f9093"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"83c1b221-c907-6b4d-aecf-5d6f1535e6fa"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
